    "text": "<p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/39900c3a-15d7-4117-b854-0eca8f65f3da-image.png\" style=\"width: 113px; height: 116px;\" /></p><p>Intramolecular <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></math>-bonding</p><p>thus it is more volatile due to intramolecular <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></math>-bonding.</p><p>Melting point of o-nitrophenol is higher because of closed packing and not because of hydrogen bonding.</p>",
